From: CipherScope <dev@cipherscope.io>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:14:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 71/77] test: sign and verify SLH-DSA-SHA2-128s in the
 functional test framework

- test_framework/crypto/slhdsa128s.py implements SLH-DSA-SHA2-128s of
  FIPS 205: key generation, pure and internal signing and verification.
  It is written for this framework from the standard, for this one
  parameter set, and shares no code with the slhdsa-c library the node
  uses, so that each checks the other. It passes NIST ACVP-Server's
  SLH-DSA-SHA2-128s keyGen (10), sigVer (28, external pure and internal)
  and sigGen (28, deterministic and randomized) vectors, and its
  deterministic signature on the fixture of slhdsa128s_tests is the one
  @noble/post-quantum 0.7.1 made. A signature takes a few seconds: it
  hashes from a SHA-256 state that has absorbed the PK.seed block, as FIPS
  205 allows, and builds each tree once.
- test_framework/p2mr_slhdsa128s.py builds the leaf SLH1, the tree, the
  signature chunks and the signature message of OP_CHECKSLHDSA128S.
